<p>Britain’s House of Commons was set to vote on April 28 on whether to refer Prime Minister Keir Starmer to the Committee of Privileges over claims he misled lawmakers about the appointment of Peter Mandelson as UK ambassador to Washington. Speaker Lindsay Hoyle approved a request from Conservative leader Kemi Badenoch for a debate and vote; Reuters reported that a finding that Starmer knowingly misled Parliament would likely make his position untenable. The row centers on Starmer’s statements that “full due process” was followed and that “no pressure whatsoever” was placed on officials during Mandelson’s vetting. Mandelson was dismissed in September after his relationship with convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein was found to be deeper than previously known; reports also said a security vetting body had recommended against granting clearance before Foreign Office officials overruled it without telling Starmer. Morgan McSweeney, Starmer’s former chief of staff, told MPs he had made a “serious error of judgment” by advising the appointment and said he asked officials to move “at pace” but not to skip steps or act improperly. Former Foreign Office chief Philip Barton declined to endorse Starmer’s “full due process” claim, told the Foreign Affairs Committee it was unusual to announce the appointment before security vetting was complete, and said Starmer knew of the risks around Mandelson’s association with Epstein.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/S90LRs_Ir9BGg_T9hTvZqXOU-TOTPhDBImBLYewWUzxmnnCkpQnPBI-icGSd_H2cQYcjxOw8XEn0E2bLBnz5WlRqCR1XtdixMkOMsqmgiKEdvriBlSFQfY1Amxlpt93uWt5WLVbGApYPkWDVSRxr2ihhpGkgZuus-uMbyoHoZ7dWIZcsAZBVHkElDmzG5V1PQ1-OhlsNRdltjSp8eHBHoq-ueLAaQTpme1GB90dMDj0BzJzFcfrFemSPWV59Z5xXWLiyCXHsnFPzmcJDiA' alt='Former No. 10 chief of staff Morgan McSweeney appears before the Foreign Affairs Committee at the Houses of Parliament in London on April 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Labour response: Starmer urged Labour MPs to vote against the referral motion, while Downing Street called the opposition push a “desperate political stunt” before local elections on May 7.</li><li>Process dispute: Barton told MPs Downing Street appeared “uninterested” in the vetting process beyond completing practical steps quickly enough for Mandelson to arrive in Washington by President Trump’s inauguration.</li><li>Security clearance: Barton and Olly Robbins told MPs the Cabinet Office initially argued Mandelson did not need developed vetting because he was a peer and privy counsellor, a position the Cabinet Office denied.</li><li>Washington politics: McSweeney said the ambassador choice would probably have differed if Kamala Harris had won the U.S. election; Starmer wanted the appointment completed before Trump’s inauguration.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Morgan McSweeney: McSweeney said Mandelson had not given the “full truth” about his relationship with Epstein, and described later details of that relationship as “like a knife through my soul.” (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/czx26yz7kxzo'>BBC</a>, <a href='https://www.standard.co.uk/news/politics/peter-mandelson-security-vetting-foreign-office-keir-starmer-vote-b1280236.html'>The Standard</a>)</li><li>Philip Barton: Barton said he received no direct calls from McSweeney while permanent under-secretary and that his limited interactions with him were in general meetings with others present. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/apr/28/keir-starmer-labour-peter-mandelson-vetting-morgan-mcsweeney-kemi-badenoch-vote-uk-politics-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Kemi Badenoch: Badenoch accused Labour MPs who obeyed the whip against the referral of “acting like sheep,” framing the vote as a test of whether Starmer would face outside scrutiny. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/apr/28/keir-starmer-labour-peter-mandelson-vetting-morgan-mcsweeney-kemi-badenoch-vote-uk-politics-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Downing Street: No. 10 published a previously confidential memo to rebut the claim that Starmer misled MPs over Mandelson’s appointment. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/apr/27/keir-starmer-peter-mandelson-inquiry-speaker-shoplifting-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/apr/28/keir-starmer-labour-peter-mandelson-vetting-morgan-mcsweeney-kemi-badenoch-vote-uk-politics-latest-news-updates'>Starmer faces harsh criticism from his own MPs as members debate referring him to privileges committee – UK politics live</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/uk-pms-former-chief-of-staff-says-he-was-wrong-to-encourage-mandelson-appointment'>Ex-aide backs British PM Starmer over Mandelson appointment</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/uk-leader-starmer-faces-pressure-mandelson-ambassador-appointment-132443252'>UK leader Starmer faces more pressure over Mandelson ambassador appointment</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e564ba59-1e9f-45fd-8ce4-d7576f31a656'>Mandelson appointment ‘serious error of judgment’, Morgan McSweeney tells MPs</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/uk-secrets-lies-7-takeaways-marathon-peter-mandelson-vetting-hearing/'>Secrets and ‘lies’: 7 takeaways from marathon Mandelson vetting hearing</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995668/uk-pm-may-face-probe-for-misleading-parliament-on-mandelson'>UK PM may face probe for ‘misleading’ parliament on Mandelson</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-uk-starmer-mandelson-appointment/'>Starmer’s former aide takes responsibility for advising Mandelson’s appointment</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.perthnow.com.au/news/politics/ex-aide-backs-uks-starmer-over-